  "is_compositional": true,
  "compositional_evidence": "Stage A divides each barcode's count by the sum over all barcodes in the same sample; stage B re-closes the input-normalised ratios to 100. The SI prints 'Total (%) = 100' on every column of both stages. A value is therefore a SHARE of a pool, not an amount: it moves when any other pool member moves, and it is not comparable to a value from a pool of different membership.",
